WEBVTT

00:00:00.102 --> 00:00:05.305
This example shows another use for null if Suppose
we want to

00:00:05.331 --> 00:00:09.856
calculate the percentage of a bill that has been
paid Normally we

00:00:09.882 --> 00:00:13.902
divide amount paid by bill amount But what happens
if the bill

00:00:13.928 --> 00:00:19.469
amount is zero Division by zero causes a problem
Here we use

00:00:19.495 --> 00:00:23.889
null if on the bill amount If the denominator is
zero null

00:00:23.915 --> 00:00:28.735
if returns null instead The result of the
calculation then becomes null

00:00:29.018 --> 00:00:34.209
which tells us the percentage is not computable Run
the SQL in

00:00:34.235 --> 00:00:38.721
the browser and inspect the percent paid column You
can also copy

00:00:38.747 --> 00:00:44.559
it into pgAdmin Notice that null does not mean zero
percent It

00:00:44.585 --> 00:00:49.971
means we could not meaningfully calculate the ratio
That distinction is important

00:00:49.997 --> 00:00:51.956
when preparing data for analysis
